From: Amir <gilaniamirhossein@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:08:48 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] proxy mode: real direct-bypass in SOCKS5 frontend +
 working per-flow relay
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- socks5_server (was dead code, now declared): Socks5ServerConfig gains
  direct_bypass — Bypass flows (IP rule, domain rule, or bypass-DNS
  query) are relayed by the frontend itself over the normal internet
  instead of answering SOCKS error 0x02 (which only iOS retries).
  Domain-name targets are now also matched against the bypass rules
  (previously only IP literals were decided).
- flow_connector: perform_handshake/send_target_address made public and
  fixed — target frames must be binary RatchetMessage (not JSON) and
  1KB-padded (the server unpads before parsing); both bugs made the very
  first post-handshake message fail. New relay_flow() provides the
  complete per-flow path (TLS+WS+X3DH+target+bidirectional copy) for
  self-contained SOCKS5 hosts.
